#== News

== About me
I am a postdoctoral researcher jointly affiliated with the [https://statistics.berkeley.edu/ Department of Statistics] at University of California, Berkeley, and the [https://www.icsi.berkeley.edu/ International Computer Science Institute], working with [https://www.stat.berkeley.edu/~mmahoney/index.html Michael Mahoney]. I received my Ph.D. in Mathematics from the University of California San Diego, where I was advised by [https://math.ucsd.edu/people/profiles/ioana-dumitriu Ioana Dumitriu] and [https://mathweb.ucsd.edu/~tkemp/ Todd Kemp].
 

== Research
My current research focuses on developing the mathematical and computational foundations of artificial intelligence using tools from high-dimensional probability and numerical linear algebra.
- Deep Learning Theory and Foundations of AI
- Randomized Numerical Linear Algebra and Optimization in LLM
- Random Matrix Theory 



